  "units": "minimum efficiency, percent, at the per-unit test load; kVA = nameplate rating; BIL in kV",
  "note": "All table values were parsed from the eCFR XML of 431.196 and checked against a text dump of the same XML. The 2029 tables (a)(3), (b)(3), (b)(4), (c)(3) were also compared with the regulatory text printed in the final rule (89 FR 29834) and match. Oddity recorded, not corrected: in Table 6 to paragraph (b)(3) (liquid-immersed, not submersible, on or after 2029-04-23) the three-phase 500 kVA minimum (99.38) is lower than 300 kVA (99.42), and 3750/5000 kVA (99.54/99.53) are lower than 2500 kVA (99.55). The final rule prints the same values; its preamble splits three-phase liquid-immersed units into equipment class 2A (15 to less than 500 kVA, about a 20 percent loss reduction) and 2B (500 kVA and above, about 5 percent), which explains the step. Linear interpolation between 300 and 500 kVA therefore gives values between 99.42 and 99.38, as the interpolation text of the rule requires. The eCFR captions the 2016 low-voltage dry-type table as Table 2 to Paragraph (a)(1) although it sits in paragraph (a)(2); it is recorded here as the (a)(2) table. Table 7 (submersible, 2029) has the same values as Table 5. Paragraph (d) (mining transformers) is reserved: no standard. Blank cells in the medium-voltage dry-type tables are null: the rule gives no minimum there. Pre-2016 tables carry no table number in the eCFR. A 2026 DOE review of the 2029 levels has been reported in secondary sources only; the eCFR snapshot above still shows the 2029 tables."
 },
